* ==================================================================
* trace2_otft.sub  -  p-type organic TFT compact model for Tortoise
* ==================================================================
* Smooth, symmetric model from subthreshold to saturation:
*
*   sp(x)   = S * ln(1 + exp(x/S)),   S = 2 * SS / ln(10)
*   I(s->d) = (beta/2) * [ sp(V_si - V_g - Vth)^2 - sp(V_di - V_g - Vth)^2 ]
*             + W * JOFF * tanh(V_si,di / 0.1 V)
*   beta    = MU * CI * W / L
*
* Contact resistance RCW/W is split equally between source and drain.
* Reference implementation: verification/otft_model.py (identical equations; not included in this release).
*
* Usage (corner parameters come from trace2_otft.lib):
*   .include ../models/trace2_otft.sub
*   .lib ../models/trace2_otft.lib lab            (or: printed)
*   X1 drain gate source potft W=80 L=5            (W, L in micrometres)
*   X2 drain gate source potft W=80 L=5 DVTH=0.05  (per-device |Vth| offset, V)
*
* Units: MU cm^2/Vs, CI F/cm^2, SS V/dec, RCW ohm*cm, JOFF A/um, VTH0 V (|Vth|), LOV um
* NOT modelled: Vg-dependent mobility and contact resistance, channel-length
* modulation, traps/hysteresis, bias-stress drift, noise, temperature.
* Capacitances are linear (Ci*W*(L/2 + LOV) per side).
* ==================================================================
.subckt potft d g s W=10 L=5 DVTH=0
.param vth   = {VTH0 + DVTH}
.param sw    = {2*SS/ln(10)}
.param beta  = {MU*CI*W/L}
.param rc2   = {max(RCW/(W*1e-4)/2, 1e-3)}
.param cside = {CI*1e-8*W*(L/2 + LOV)}
Rcs s si {rc2}
Rcd d di {rc2}
B1 si di I = {beta/2} * ( ({sw}*ln(1+exp((v(si,g)-{vth})/{sw})))^2
+                       - ({sw}*ln(1+exp((v(di,g)-{vth})/{sw})))^2 )
+            + {W*JOFF}*tanh(v(si,di)/0.1)
Cgs g si {cside}
Cgd g di {cside}
Rleak si di 1e14
.ends potft
